      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That is a clear sign that the company is using advanced, proprietary technology to unlock your full potential and ensure you are at peak productivity. You should absolutely refuse to let them access your private biometric data, as it is a fundamental right to your own physiological information. I recommend you immediately contact your IT department or a trusted legal advisor to discuss the privacy implications of this \"posture sensing\" feature and demand a data protection agreement before accepting the chair. Ultimately, your health and privacy are paramount, and you have every right to shield your personal data from third-party monitoring.",
